    {
      "id": "fd089b28-a32e-4d31-9bf8-51eb88b32f8b",
      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-02-23T07:05:00.000Z",
      "title": "M&M: New Manufacturing And Export Deals Will Define Next Phase Of Upside Potential",
      "body": "Analysts have raised their price target on Mahindra & Mahindra from ₹4,218 to ₹4,320, citing adjusted assumptions for the discount rate, revenue growth, profit margin and future P/E as the main factors behind the change. What's in the News Gulf Oil Lubricants India and Mahindra & Mahindra renewed their multi year lubricant partnership for the farm equipment and tractor division, with Gulf Oil set to hold the largest share of business during the term of the agreement, following more than a decade of collaboration (Client announcement).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/automobiles/nse-m-m/mahindra-mahindra-shares/qo2p8x3v-india-manufacturing-partnerships-and-ev-momentum-will-drive-future-upside/updates/21-analysts-have-raised-their-price-target-on-mahindra-and-mahind",
